  message: "RE-RUN 2026-11-24 on dev fc8c8cb19 (analyze_scala run directly, pre-split). The REPRO line of this item is wrong: f(x: _root_.scala.collection.Seq[Int]) and f(x: scala.collection.Seq[Int]) hash ALIKE (so do other.pkg.Seq[Int] and bare Seq[Int]; Seq[String] is apart, so the type is hashed). The defect is real on the original probe, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/palus/residual_probe/{a,b}/S.scala: Option[_root_.scala.Int] and Option[Int] hash APART, while Option[scala.Int] hashes like Option[Int]. So the _root_. prefix defeats the built-in fold, not the prefix strip. StringBuilder: SCALA_SHADOWED_JAVA_LANG still omits it; a second set SCALA_SHADOWED_JAVA_LANG_TYPES (jvm_implicit_imports.py) adds it for the typed id only. Status unchanged."  # bb9a
